{#
  T-2.04 — the theme's only icon entry point.

  Usage:
    {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'shopping-bag' } %}
    {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'heart', size: 'lg' } %}
    {% include 'components.ui.icon' with { name: 'cancel', label: 'إغلاق'|trans } %}

  Parameters:
    name   required — the sicon glyph without its prefix, e.g. 'shopping-bag'
    size   xs · sm · md (default) · lg · xl
    label  an accessible name. Supply it ONLY when the icon carries meaning no
           adjacent text already carries. Omitting it is the common case.
    class  extra utility classes

  WHY THIS EXISTS. Icons are written as <i class="sicon-…"> in 52 distinct
  places across the theme and **not one of them carries aria-hidden**. An icon
  font renders through a private-use-area codepoint, so a screen reader either
  announces nothing useful or announces garbage — and where the icon is the
  only content of a button, the control has no accessible name at all. Routing
  every icon through here makes the accessible default automatic: decorative
  unless someone deliberately names it.

  THE DEFAULT IS aria-hidden, AND THAT IS THE CORRECT DEFAULT. Most icons in
  this design sit beside their own label — the cart icon next to «السلة», the
  chevron beside a link. Naming those makes a screen reader say everything
  twice. `label` is the exception, for a genuinely standalone control.

  Colour is deliberately not set. An icon font inherits `currentColor`, so the
  icon takes the colour of whatever it sits in and needs no token of its own.

  THE ICON FONT IS RETAINED, not replaced with an SVG sprite — ruled by the
  project owner 2026-08-06. `master.twig` already loads sallaicons.css from the
  CDN, all 52 icons in use come from it, and only 2 local SVGs exist. Replacing
  it would mean redrawing 52 glyphs to gain a sprite the theme does not need.
  The acceptance criterion's "single sprite" is therefore satisfied by the font
  itself: one file, one request, one source.
#}
{% set ui_icon_sizes = {
    'xs': 'text-xs',
    'sm': 'text-sm',
    'md': 'text-base',
    'lg': 'text-xl',
    'xl': 'text-2xl'
} %}
{% set ui_icon_size = ui_icon_sizes[size|default('md')]|default('text-base') %}

<i class="ui-icon sicon-{{ name }} {{ ui_icon_size }} {{ class|default('') }}"
   {% if label is defined and label is not empty %}role="img" aria-label="{{ label }}"{% else %}aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}></i>
